ADDENDA <Act No. 20927, Apr. 22, 2025>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation; provided, the amended provisions of Articles 10-2 and 50 shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability to comprehensive policy plans for persons with disabilities)
The amended provisions of Article 10-2 shall begin to apply to cases where comprehensive policy plans for persons with disabilities are formulated or modified after the same amended provisions enter into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to payment of allowances for children with disabilities)
The amended provisions of Article 10-2 shall begin to apply to cases where comprehensive policy plans for persons with disabilities are formulated or modified after the same amended provisions enter into force.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning eligibility requirements to take national examination for speech-language pathologists)
A person who, before this Act enters into force, completed courses related to speech-language rehabilitation under the previous Article 72-2(5) at a graduate school (limited to a graduate school established in a cyber college; hereinafter the same shall apply) or a cyber college under the Higher Education Act and obtained a master's degree, bachelor's degree, or associate degree in a relevant department, and a person who, as at the time this Act enters into force, is enrolled in a department related to speech-language rehabilitation at a graduate school or cyber college under the Higher Education Act (limited to a person who was admitted before October 31, 2024), who completes courses related to speech-language rehabilitation under the previous Article 72-2(5) and obtains a master's degree, bachelor's degree, or associate degree in a relevant department by February 28, 2026 shall, if he or she completes field practicum courses by February 28, 2029 in accordance with the standards prescribed by Prime Ministerial Decree, be deemed eligible to take the national examination for speech-language pathologists under this Act, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 72-2.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning acquisition of qualification as speech-language pathologist)
A person who, as at the time this Act enters into force, completed courses related to speech-language rehabilitation under the previous Article 72-2(5) at a graduate school or cyber college under the Higher Education Act, obtained a master's degree, bachelor's degree, or associate degree in a relevant department, and thereafter acquired qualification as a speech-language pathologist shall be deemed to have acquired qualification as a speech-language pathologist under this Act.

